        "title": "Stop forcing a GitHub credential helper for Git operations",
        "body": "Use normal Git authentication behavior by default.\n\nDo not inject `credential.helper=!gh auth git-credential` into Git commands unless a concrete workflow explicitly requires that override.\n\nConceptually:\n\n```text\nGitWeave invokes git\n  \u2193\nnormal Git config / SSH / credential helpers apply\n  \u2193\nGit succeeds or returns its real error\n```\n\nGitHub System Actions may continue to use the `gh` CLI for GitHub API operations. This issue is specifically about Git transport authentication for `git fetch`, `git push`, `git ls-remote`, and similar commands.\n\nIf a user wants GitHub CLI credentials to back Git transport, that should come from their normal Git/GitHub configuration rather than a hidden GitWeave override.\n\nThis change implements the behavior above with focused regression coverage and documentation.\n\nValidation: deterministic regression tests and independent GitWeave review; GitHub CI on the published changes.\n\nCloses #41."
      }
    },
